(II)--a सूक्त of the साम Samhita1;
1: वा. 9. ५०; २१. ७५ and ७८.
recited in tank ritual;
2: M. ५८. ३७.
from the south face of ब्रह्मा.
3: Br. II. 8. ५१; Vi. 1. 5. ५४.

(I)--a son of Angiras by सुनीपा; (also प्रजापति-वा। प्।); a ब्रह्मिष्ठ famous in स्वारो- चिषान्तर; a sage of the स्वारोचिष epoch,
1: भा. IV. 1. ३५; १७. 9. 8. M. १९२. १०; १९६. 5. १९, २४. वा. ५२. ७७; ५३. ३३; ५९. ९०, १३१; ८५. १००; ९८. २४ and २७.
born of Phalguni in चक्षुषान्तर; a Mantra-ब्राह्मण; identified with Bha- गवान्,
2: भा. XI. १६. २२; M. २४५. ८६; २४९. ११.
lord of विश्रवस् and Angiras; sister, Yogasiddha, wife of प्रभास; wife तारा who was taken away by Soma; she came back after शिव's war with him and ब्रह्मा's inter- vention; father of Kaca and भरद्वाज;
3: भा. IX. १४. 4; M. २३. ३०, ४७; २६. 3; वा. ६५. १०३; ७०. 4; ७६. 1 and २५; Vi. IV. 6. १०.
had sexual [page२-501+ ५२] intercourse with Mamata (brother's wife), when she was pregnant; cursed the baby in the womb for obstructing the entry of his semen. भरद्वाज was born who was brought up by the Maruts;
4: भा. IX. २०. ३६-9; M. ४८. ३३-41; ४९. १५. Vi. IV. १९. १६; वा. ९९. ३७; १०३. ५९; १०६. ५०.
appointed Purohita of the Gods and got back to life the Gods killed by the Asuras;
5: Ib. IX. २४. ४५; २५. 9. १२; वा. 2. १९; 3. 4; ३८. ४४.
had faith in क्रियायोग;
6: भा. XI. २७. 2.
served as calf for the sages (milked the cow- earth-वा। प्।) to milk the Vedic lore from the earth and got the essence of tapas; saciva of Indra; caused illusion for ^7 Ib. IV. १८. १४; M. १०. १७; वा. ६२. १३८ and १७७. Rajo's sons and got back the place for Indra;
8: भा. V. २४. २४; M. २९. ११; वा. ५३. ६७; Vi. IV. 9. १७-22.
wielded over- lordship over Indra and was the cause of his योगक्षेम;
9: वा. ८४. १५; ९२. ९१.
master of Mantras;
१०: M. ४७. ८१.
finding शुक्र engaged for ten years with Jayanti, Br. took the guise of शुक्र and acted as शुक्र to the Asuras; when शुक्र spoke of the deceit, they would not listen to him and hence were cursed; बृहस्पति threw off his guise and went to his place;
११: Ib. ४७. १८१-205.
appeared before the Asuras in the guise of काव्य;
१२: वा. ९७. १०६, १२१.
fought with उशनस् or शुक्र in the देवासुर war;
१३: भा VIII. १०. ३३.
advised Indra besieged by Bali, to abandon the city and await better times
१४: Ib. VIII. १५. २८-31.
was not accorded due welcome by Indra in his pride and hence बृहस्पति abandoned the Devas when the Asuras rose up in arms against them; after consulting him on तारक's advance, Indra resolved on war;
१५: Ib. VI. 7. ७९ and १६-19; M. १४८. ६२-76.
blessed उमा with a son; blessed the Deva host in the तारकामय.
१६: Ib. १५४. ५०७; १७४. ५२.

(II)--a planet; three-fourth of शुक्र (भार्- gava वा। प्।) in size; possesses १२ rays;
1: Br. II. २३. ८५; M. १२८. ४८, ६४; वा. ५३. ८७.
has a golden chariot drawn by 8 white (red-वा। प्।) horses;
2: M. १२७. 5; वा. ५२. ७७-9; Vi. II. १२. १९.
traverses each sign in one full year; generally favourable to the Brahmanas; a good ग्रह;
3: भा. V. २२. १५; XII. 2. २४; M. २६४. 8.
on the right a bad omen;
4: Ib. १६३. ३९.
his place above [page२-502+ ३१] Budha;
5: वा. ५३. ९७.
in Simha, every twelve years;
6: Ib. ८३. ४२.
stands above अन्गा- raka at a distance of २००० yojanas and below शनि.
7: Ib. १०१. १३३; Vi. II. 7. 9.

(III)--a ऋषि;
1: M. १४५. ९२.
heard the भागवत from सान्खायन;
2: भा. III. 8. 8.
teacher of Uddava;
3: Ib. III. 1. २५; IV. 7. ६०.
went to स्यमन्तपञ्- caka to see कृष्ण,
4: Ib. X. ८४. 4.
went with कृष्ण to मिथिला;
5: Ib. X. ८६. १८.
advised Jana- mejaya to give up Sarpasatra; by doing this he honoured the sage.
6: Ib. XII. 6. २३-28
